{"n": 946, "w": 1000, "h": 764, "img": "946.webp", "text": "3251072\n\n30 51793\n\n51-319\n\nAdjust window by turning adjusting\npads unt! window bears uniformly In\nbody opening.\n\nLift out window with Special Tool\n513.010 and cut off tabs on clips all\naround.\n\nShape of Cement Bead:\n\na 10mm (0.394\")\nb 12mm (0.472*)\n\ntf necessary, make a sample bead be-\nfore cementing. Catridge must be per-\npendicular to window surface. Check\nfor uniform feed and pulling speed\nduring application of cement.\n\nNote:\n\nUse a cartridge gun* (pneumatic or\nelectric) to produce uniform beads of\ncement.\n\nCheck the cement's date of expiry!\n\n* Source of Supply: HWB\n\n30 51 616\n\nPraduce cement bead (1) on window\nall around.\n\nDistance A to edge of window = ap-\nprox. 5 mm (0.197\").\n\nFit In and press on window carefully\nwith Special Tool 51 3 040 (used In\nconjunction with Special Tool 51 3 010).\n\n(Check for uniform spacing between\nbody and ornamental strip all around.\n\nPreload window lightly with a strap.\n\nImportant!\n\nAlways remove dirt from residual ce-\niment with cleaning benzol before the\ncement has hardened, Don't press out\nwindow again for this purpose.\n\nNote:\n\nLeaks can be detected by spraying\nwater underneath sealing lip or with an\nultrasonic leak detector,\n\n(Leaks can be repaired with a corres-\nponding nozzle (repair kit*).\n\n* Source of Supply: HWB", "words": [["3251072", 0.1891, 0.7255, 0.2437, 0.7388], ["30", 0.2032, 0.9735, 0.2144, 0.9828], ["51793", 0.2174, 0.9722, 0.2467, 0.9815], ["51-319", 0.459, 0.0231, 0.5268, 0.047], ["Adjust", 0.2685, 0.0787, 0.3038, 0.0933], ["window", 0.3069, 0.0787, 0.3483, 0.0893], ["by", 0.3514, 0.0787, 0.3645, 0.0933], ["turning", 0.3675, 0.0774, 0.406, 0.0919], ["adjusting", 0.41, 0.0774, 0.459, 0.0919], ["pads", 0.2685, 0.0946, 0.2947, 0.1098], ["unt!", 0.2988, 0.0946, 0.322, 0.1071], ["window", 0.3261, 0.0946, 0.3665, 0.1071], ["bears", 0.3696, 0.0946, 0.3999, 0.1071], ["uniformly", 0.4029, 0.09